seg-3ba911ed9541 = The solution file RTKLIB's <c1/> and RTKPOST write. Read: the time (calendar <c2/>, or GPS week and seconds of week), the position (latitude and longitude in degrees with height, or ECEF X/Y/Z converted to geodetic) and the number of satellites. The time scale in the column header (<c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/>) is carried in the label. Degrees-minutes-seconds files are refused. Lines starting <c6/> are header lines.

# text
# c1: format = "novatel"
seg-24ebc9ea6e4e = NovAtel OEM7 (<c1/>)

# text
# c1: #BESTPOSA,...*crc
# c2: AA 44 12
seg-b73d1465ed67 = ASCII (<c1/>) and binary (<c2/> header) logs, mixed freely. Layouts follow the public OEM7 documentation (docs.novatel.com): the message headers, the 32-bit CRC and the field tables of three logs. Records whose CRC does not match are skipped and counted.

